# The words of the window of FreeSynergy Forms, English (ADR 0057: MessageFormat 2). Every id needs a German twin in de.mf2.
app-name = FreeSynergy Forms
app-tagline = Goal: Ask questions, collect answers and read the result, and an anonymous answer is really anonymous, not just labelled so.
app-basics = This is the first version, the basics: the program starts, the server runs and the core behind it is ready. The window for forms comes next.
soon = coming soon
state-connected = The server answers and speaks the contract {$contract}.
state-down = No server is running: {$reason}
state-contract = This frontend does not fit the server: {$reason}
state-hint-down = Start the program with the command `fs-forms`; it starts the server and this window.
state-hint-contract = Install a matching version of FreeSynergy Forms; the window below only shows what is planned.
today-title = What it can do today
today-1 = Opens this window with `fs-forms`, finds its server and checks that both speak the same contract version.
today-2 = The server `fs-forms serve` answers what it offers (nothing yet) and the support report; everything else says "unimplemented".
today-3 = Says plainly what is not there yet; nothing here pretends to work.
today-4 = The core (surveys with questions and conditions, anonymous ballots in a separate box, results in batches, counting methods, CSV export, widening over groups) exists as a library and is not connected to this window yet.
coming-title = What comes
coming-intro = Everything below is not there yet. The first ones are the plan for the next versions.
coming-1 = A list of my surveys with name, state and number of answers, and a search; create, rename, duplicate and delete (the warning says that the answers go with it).
coming-2 = An editor for questions with a preview: add, change, move and delete questions; single and multiple choice, drop-down, short and long text, number, date and time; required questions and checks of the input.
coming-3 = States draft, open, closed and archived, with start and end.
coming-4 = Answering in a window of its own: fill in, save a draft, continue later, submit; a test answer in the preview without saving.
coming-5 = The level of anonymity is chosen and shown to the person who answers, with its limits stated.
coming-6 = The result as a summary with charts and the number of answers, and a CSV export.
coming-7 = Inviting: choose people and groups; at first only invited people can answer.
coming-8 = A public link without an account, protected against mass answers, and embedding in other programs: comes with the server part. Planned, not scheduled.
coming-9 = Date polls (Doodle style) belong to the program Decisions; Forms supplies the input fields that are embedded there.
menu-program = Forms
menu-new = New survey
menu-open = Open
menu-export = Export as CSV
screen-start = Start
screen-comes = What comes
status-ready = Ready
